    "path": "buoyant_kernel::expressions::VariadicExpressionOp::Array",
    "name": "Array",
    "owner": "buoyant_kernel::expressions::VariadicExpressionOp",
    "crate": "buoyant_kernel",
    "version": "1.0.0+58f07cd6",
    "kind": "variant",
    "signature": "Array",
    "docs": "Construct an Array by evaluating each input expression. For example, the expression\n`Array(1, (1 + 2), col(\"my_int_col\"))` evaluates to the array\n`[1, 3, <my_int_col value>]` per row. All inputs must share the same element type.\nRequires at least one element; the element type is inferred from the inputs.\n\nFor static array literals whose elements are all compile-time constants, use\n[`Scalar::Array`] instead. The difference is that `Array` is evaluated at runtime, while\n`Scalar::Array` is evaluated at compile time.",
